The JPEG decoder and encoder
============================

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.

The JPEG code in jpeg-shared/, jpeg-decoder/ and jpeg-encoder/ is a
translation into Whackford of parts of libjpeg-turbo 3.2.0
(https://libjpeg-turbo.org), which is based on the Independent JPEG Group's
software. The decoder reproduces djpeg's output byte for byte and the
encoder reproduces cjpeg's, so their algorithms, constants and rounding
follow that source closely, and the .wack files name the libjpeg-turbo
source files they follow. Among them:

  decoding        jdhuff.c, jdphuff.c, jdarith.c, jaricom.c, jdcoefct.c,
                  jidctint.c, jdsample.c, jdmainct.c, jdcolor.c, jdapistd.c,
                  jdmaster.c, wrppm.c
  encoding        jchuff.c, jstdhuff.c, jcparam.c, jcmarker.c, jcicc.c, jdicc.c,
                  jfdctint.c, jcdctmgr.c, jccoefct.c, jcprepct.c, jcsample.c,
                  jccolor.c, jcmaster.c, rdppm.c
  shared          jutils.c, jdct.h, jdatadst.c

Changes from the original files: the code is rewritten in Whackford rather
than copied; it is restructured into words with declared stack effects and
tests; input that libjpeg accepts or repairs is often refused instead (the
refusal codes and limits in jpeg-shared/limits.wack and
jpeg-encoder/jpeg/elimits.wack); only the integer DCTs are implemented, and
the encoder writes one baseline profile; the EXIF orientation reader, the
ICC profile checks and the whole sanitiser program (jpeg-encoder/clean.wack)
are new. The test tools jpeg-encoder/tools/fdct_oracle.c, prep_oracle.c and
rescale_oracle.c compile against the libjpeg-turbo source to produce
expected values; they contain none of it.

